<title>IRAN: Fourth English daily launched in Iran.</title>
<headline>Fourth English daily launched in Iran.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran Daily, the Islamic republic's fourth English-language newspaper, was launched on Wednesday, two days before the country's presidential election.</p>
<p>The eight-page tabloid said it would concentrate on domestic and regional economic affairs. The main story in its inaugural issue was on the countdown to Friday's poll.</p>
<p>The newspaper is produced by the official Islamic Republic News Agency (IRNA). It competes with Iran News, Kayhan International and Tehran Times.</p>
